From: Nex package maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] add the transient configuration tier and drop /usr/etc

Every distrobox command sources the same fixed list of configuration files, so
a later file overrides an earlier one. The list had no /run entry, which left a
boot-time tool with nowhere to put temporary machine policy, and it read
/usr/etc, which is not a vendor location on a system that keeps package
defaults below /usr/share and /usr/lib.

Insert /run/distrobox/distrobox.conf between the package defaults and the
administrator file, and drop the /usr/etc entry. The per-user files and the
DBX_* environment variables keep their existing priority above all of them.

diff -urN a/distrobox-assemble b/distrobox-assemble
--- a/distrobox-assemble
+++ b/distrobox-assemble
@@ -93,8 +93,8 @@
 	${nix_config_file}
 	/usr/share/distrobox/distrobox.conf
 	/usr/share/defaults/distrobox/distrobox.conf
-	/usr/etc/distrobox/distrobox.conf
 	/usr/local/share/distrobox/distrobox.conf
+	/run/distrobox/distrobox.conf
 	/etc/distrobox/distrobox.conf
 	${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-"${HOME}/.config"}/distrobox/distrobox.conf
 	${HOME}/.distroboxrc
